<title>NETHERLANDS: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stocks mixed.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stocks mixed.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			 3/4/97		  20/3/97		5/4/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	    600			550	     500-525</p>
<p>    Naphtha		75			125		    50</p>
<p>    Gas oil   1,750-1,800		    1,725		 1,800</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	300-325			350		   300</p>
<p>    Jet kero	  10-15			 15		    10</p>
<p>Gasoline stocks rose slightly ahead of the traditional driving season. Throughput of cargoes and barges was rapid.</p>
<p>Naphtha stocks dipped. Throughput was also rapid.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks rose as incoming cargoes outweighed barge market departures.</p>
<p>Fuel oil stocks slipped with almost no incoming product. German refiners took out straight-run product and some cracked material went to the bunker sector.</p>
<p>Some jet fuel left for the aviation sector.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom, +31 20 504 5004</p>
